    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    from itertools import product\n    \n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    \n    # Parse input\n    N = int(data[0])\n    D = list(map(int, data[1:N+1]))\n    L1, C1, K1 = map(int, data[N+1:N+4])\n    L2, C2, K2 = map(int, data[N+4:N+7])\n    \n    # For each section, precompute the possible ways to cover it\n    # (num_sensors_type1, num_sensors_type2, cost)\n    section_options = []\n    \n    for d in D:\n        options = []\n        # Try all possible combinations of sensors for this section\n        max_sensors1 = min(K1, (d + L1 - 1) // L1 + 1)  # upper bound\n        max_sensors2 = min(K2, (d + L2 - 1) // L2 + 1)  # upper bound\n        \n        for s1 in range(max_sensors1 + 1):\n            remaining = max(0, d - s1 * L1)\n            s2 = (remaining + L2 - 1) // L2 if remaining > 0 else 0\n            \n            if s2 <= K2 and s1 * L1 + s2 * L2 >= d:\n                cost = s1 * C1 + s2 * C2\n                options.append((s1, s2, cost))\n        \n        if not options:\n            print(-1)\n            return\n            \n        section_options.append(options)\n    \n    # Now we need to find the combination across all sections\n    # that minimizes total cost while respecting K1 and K2 constraints\n    min_cost = float('inf')\n    \n    # Use dynamic programming approach\n    # dp[i][used1][used2] = minimum cost to cover first i sections\n    # using 'used1' type-1 sensors and 'used2' type-2 sensors\n    \n    # We'll use a dictionary-based DP to avoid using too much memory\n    dp = {(0, 0): 0}  # (used1, used2) -> cost\n    \n    for options in section_options:\n        new_dp = {}\n        \n        for (used1, used2), cost_so_far in dp.items():\n            for s1, s2, add_cost in options:\n                new_used1 = used1 + s1\n                new_used2 = used2 + s2\n                \n                if new_used1 <= K1 and new_used2 <= K2:\n                    new_cost = cost_so_far + add_cost\n                    \n                    key = (new_used1, new_used2)\n                    if key not in new_dp or new_dp[key] > new_cost:\n                        new_dp[key] = new_cost\n        \n        dp = new_dp\n        \n        if not dp:\n            break\n    \n    if dp:\n        min_cost = min(dp.values())\n        print(min_cost)\n    else:\n        print(-1)\n\nsolve()\n```",
