      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    giants = []\n    index = 1\n    for _ in range(n):\n        a = int(data[index])\n        b = int(data[index + 1])\n        index += 2\n        giants.append((a, b))\n    \n    # Sort by B_i in descending order to maximize head height of the topmost giant\n    giants.sort(key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n    \n    # Stack them based on the sorted order\n    current_shoulder_height = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        a, b = giants[i]\n        current_shoulder_height += a\n        if i == n - 1:  # topmost giant\n            head_height = current_shoulder_height + b - a\n            print(head_height)\n            return\n\nsolve()\n```",
