      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef doesValidArrayExist(derived):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines whether there exists a valid binary array original that could have formed derived.\n    \n    The key insight is that for a valid original array to exist, the XOR of all elements in derived\n    must be 0. This is because each element in original appears exactly twice in the derived array\n    (once with its next element, and once when the last element is XORed with the first), so the\n    total XOR should be 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate the XOR of all elements in derived\n    total_xor = 0\n    for value in derived:\n        total_xor ^= value\n    \n    # A valid original array exists if and only if the XOR of all derived elements is 0\n    return total_xor == 0\n```",
