      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\ndef find(parent, x):\n    if parent[x] != x:\n        parent[x] = find(parent, parent[x])\n    return parent[x]\n\ndef union(parent, rank, x, y):\n    px, py = find(parent, x), find(parent, y)\n    if px == py:\n        return False\n    if rank[px] < rank[py]:\n        px, py = py, px\n    parent[py] = px\n    if rank[px] == rank[py]:\n        rank[px] += 1\n    return True\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    K = int(data[2])\n    \n    edges = []\n    index = 3\n    for _ in range(m):\n        u = int(data[index]) - 1\n        v = int(data[index+1]) - 1\n        w = int(data[index+2])\n        edges.append((w, u, v))\n        index += 3\n    \n    # We are to find the minimum cost spanning tree where cost = sum(weights) mod K\n    # Since N <= 8, we can try all possible spanning trees (which are subsets of edges of size N-1)\n    # But a better approach is to consider weighted matroid optimization with modulo K twist.\n    \n    # However, note: The cost is sum mod K. So we are not minimizing the usual MST.\n    # We want to minimize (sum of weights) mod K.\n    # Since the total number of spanning trees is manageable for N <= 8, we can iterate over all possible edge combinations of size (N-1)\n    \n    min_cost = float('inf')\n\n    # Try all combinations of M choose (N-1)\n    for subset in combinations(range(m), n-1):\n        selected_edges = [edges[i] for i in subset]\n        parent = list(range(n))\n        rank = [0] * n\n        total_weight = 0\n        count = 0\n        \n        for w, u, v in selected_edges:\n            if union(parent, rank, u, v):\n                total_weight += w\n                count += 1\n        \n        # Check if it's a spanning tree: must have exactly n-1 edges and connect all nodes\n        if count == n-1:\n            # Normalize modulo K correctly\n            cost = total_weight % K\n            if cost < min_cost:\n                min iCost = cost\n    \n    print(min_cost)\n\nmain()\n```",
