      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Parse first line\n    N = int(data[0])\n    M = int(data[1])\n    H = int(data[2])\n    K = int(data[3])\n    \n    # Parse string S\n    S = data[4]\n    \n    # Parse M item positions\n    items = set()\n    index = 5\n    for _ in range(M):\n        x = int(data[index])\n        y = int(data[index + 1])\n        items.add((x, y))\n        index += 2\n    \n    # Start position and health\n    x, y = 0, 0\n    health = H\n    \n    # Process each move\n    for i in range(N):\n        # Move based on direction\n        direction = S[i]\n        if direction == 'R':\n            x += 1\n        elif direction == 'L':\n            x -= 1\n        elif direction == 'U':\n            y += 1\n        elif direction == 'D':\n            y -= 1\n        \n        # Consume 1 health for the move\n        health -= 1\n        \n        # Check if collapsed\n        if health < 0:\n            print(\"No\")\n            return\n        \n        # Check for recovery item\n        if (x, y) in items and health < K:\n            health = K\n            # Remove the item so it can't be used again\n            items.remove((x, y))\n    \n    print(\"Yes\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
