      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumEnergy(energy, k):\n    n = len(energy)\n    # Create dp array to store maximum energy starting from each position\n    dp = [0] * n\n    \n    # Fill dp array from right to left\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        # Base case: if we're at a position where next jump goes out of bounds\n        if i + k >= n:\n            dp[i] = energy[i]\n        else:\n            # Otherwise, take current energy plus best path from next position\n            dp[i] = energy[i] + dp[i + k]\n    \n    # Return the maximum energy we can get from any starting position\n    return max(dp)\n```",
