      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countServersWithoutRequests(n, logs, x, queries):\n    # Sort logs by time\n    logs.sort(key=lambda log: log[1])\n    \n    # Create result array\n    result = []\n    \n    # For each query, count servers that didn't receive requests in the time window\n    for query in queries:\n        start_time = query - x\n        end_time = query\n        \n        # Create a set to track which servers received requests in the time window\n        servers_with_requests = set()\n        \n        # Find all logs within the time interval [start_time, end_time]\n        for server_id, time in logs:\n            if start_time <= time <= end_time:\n                servers_with_requests.add(server_id)\n            elif time > end_time:\n                # Since logs are sorted by time, we can break early\n                break\n        \n        # Count servers that didn't receive any requests\n        servers_without_requests = n - len(servers_with_requests)\n        result.append(servers_without_requests)\n    \n    return result\n```",
