      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the longest substring that doesn't contain any forbidden substring.\n\nMy approach:\n1. Use a sliding window technique\n2. For each position, expand the window while checking if any forbidden substring appears\n3. When a forbidden substring is found, shrink the window from the left\n4. Keep track of the maximum valid length found\n\nSince forbidden substrings can be of length up to 10, when I find a forbidden substring ending at position j, I need to move the left pointer to at least one position after the start of this forbidden substring.\n\n```python\ndef longestValidSubstring(word, forbidden):\n    forbidden_set = set(forbidden)\n    n = len(word)\n    left = 0\n    max_len = 0\n    \n    for right in range(n):\n        # Check if adding word[right] creates any forbidden substring\n        # We need to check all substrings ending at right that could be forbidden\n        for start in range(max(left, right - 9), right + 1):\n            substring = word[start:right + 1]\n            if substring in forbidden_set:\n                # Move left pointer to just after the start of forbidden substring\n                left = start + 1\n                break\n        \n        max_len = max(max_len, right - left + 1)\n    \n    return max_len\n```",
