    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    \n    # Read input\n    lines = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    H, W = map(int, lines[0].split())\n    \n    # Create grid\n    grid = []\n    for i in range(1, H + 1):\n        grid.append(list(lines[i]))\n    \n    # Function to check if all non-removed cookies in a row have same color\n    def check_row_markable(row_idx):\n        row = grid[row_idx]\n        colors = [c for c in row if c != '.']\n        if len(colors) < 2:\n            return False\n        return all(color == colors[0] for color in colors)\n    \n    # Function to check if all non-removed cookies in a column have same color\n    def check_col_markable(col_idx):\n        colors = [grid[i][col_idx] for i in range(H) if grid[i][col_idx] != '.']\n        if len(colors) < 2:\n            return False\n        return all(color == colors[0] for color in colors)\n    \n    # Main simulation loop\n    while True:\n        marked = set()\n        \n        # Step 1: Check rows\n        for i in range(H):\n            if check_row_markable(i):\n                # Mark all cookies in this row\n                for j in range(W):\n                    if grid[i][j] != '.':\n                        marked.add((i, j))\n        \n        # Step 2: Check columns\n        for j in range(W):\n            if check_col_markable(j):\n                # Mark all cookies in this column\n                for i in range(H):\n                    if grid[i][j] != '.':\n                        marked.add((i, j))\n        \n        # Step 3: If no cookies marked, terminate\n        if not marked:\n            break\n            \n        # Remove marked cookies\n        for i, j in marked:\n            grid[i][j] = '.'\n    \n    # Count remaining cookies\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] != '.':\n                count += 1\n                \n    print(count)\n\nsolve()\n```",
