    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to count the number of ways to distribute `n` candies among 3 children where each child gets at most `limit` candies.\n\nThis is essentially counting the number of non-negative integer solutions to:\n- x + y + z = n\n- 0 ≤ x ≤ limit\n- 0 ≤ y ≤ limit  \n- 0 ≤ z ≤ limit\n\nI can solve this by iterating through all possible values for the first two children, and then checking if the remaining amount for the third child is valid.\n\n```python\ndef distributeCandies(n, limit):\n    count = 0\n    # Iterate through all possible values for child 1 and child 2\n    for child1 in range(min(n, limit) + 1):\n        for child2 in range(min(n - child1, limit) + 1):\n            child3 = n - child1 - child2\n            # Check if child3 is within the limit and non-negative\n            if 0 <= child3 <= limit:\n                count += 1\n    return count\n```",
