      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumOperations(word, k):\n    n = len(word)\n    # Extract all k-length blocks\n    blocks = []\n    for i in range(0, n, k):\n        blocks.append(word[i:i+k])\n    \n    # Count frequency of each unique block\n    block_count = {}\n    for block in blocks:\n        block_count[block] = block_count.get(block, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Find the most frequent block\n    max_frequency = max(block_count.values())\n    \n    # Minimum operations = total blocks - blocks that already match the target\n    # We want to make all blocks equal to the most frequent one\n    return len(blocks) - max_frequency\n```",
