      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport math\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    N, D = map(int, input().split())\n    people = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        x, y = map(int, input().split())\n        people.append((x, y))\n    \n    # Initialize infection status (person 1 is infected initially)\n    infected = [False] * N\n    infected[0] = True\n    \n    # Use BFS to spread the virus\n    queue = deque([0])  # Start with person 0 (index 0)\n    \n    while queue:\n        current = queue.popleft()\n        current_x, current_y = people[current]\n        \n        # Check all other people\n        for i in range(N):\n            if infected[i]:  # Already infected\n                continue\n                \n            # Calculate Euclidean distance\n            other_x, other_y = people[i]\n            distance = math.sqrt((current_x - other_x) ** 2 + (current_y - other_y) ** 2)\n            \n            # If within distance D, infect the person\n            if distance <= D:\n                infected[i] = True\n                queue.append(i)\n    \n    # Output results\n    for i in range(N):\n        print(\"Yes\" if infected[i] else \"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
