0, 1, and 2. Among these, the answer is the string at index 2 because it has the shortest length of 6.\nFor wordsQuery[1] = \"acbfgh\", only the string at index 0 shares the longest common suffix \"fgh\". Hence it is the answer, even though the string at index 2 is shorter.\nFor wordsQuery[2] = \"acbfegh\", strings from wordsContainer that share the longest common suffix \"gh\" are at indices 0, 1, and 2. Among these, the answer is the string at index 2 because it has the shortest length of 6.\n\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= wordsContainer.length, wordsQuery.length <= 10^4\n1 <= wordsContainer[i].length <= 5 * 10^3\n1 <= wordsQuery[i].length <= 5 * 10^3\nwordsContainer[i] consists only of lowercase English letters.\nwordsQuery[i] consists only of lowercase English letters.\nSum of wordsContainer[i].length is at most 5 * 10^5.\nSum of wordsQuery[i].length is at most 5 * 10^5.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findWords(wordsContainer, wordsQuery):\n    def get_suffix(word, length):\n        return word[-length:] if length <= len(word) else \"\"\n    \n    def get_common_suffix_length(str1, str2):\n        min_len = min(len(str1), len(str2))\n        for i in range(min_len):\n            if str1[-(i+1)] != str2[-(i+1)]:\n                return i\n        return min_len\n    \n    ans = []\n    \n    # Preprocess wordsContainer to store info for each word\n    container_info = [(word, len(word), i) for i, word in enumerate(wordsContainer)]\n    \n    for query in wordsQuery:\n        best_index = 0\n        max_suffix_len = 0\n        min_length = len(wordsContainer[0])\n        \n        for i, (word, word_len, orig_idx) in enumerate(container_info):\n            suffix_len = get_common_suffix_length(word, query)\n            \n            # Update best match if this one is better\n            if suffix_len > max_suffix_len:\n                max_suffix_len = suffix_len\n                min_length = word_len\n                best_index = orig_idx\n            elif suffix_len == max_suffix_len:\n                # Same suffix length, check for shorter word\n                if word_len < min_length:\n                    min_length = word_len\n                    best_index = orig_idx\n                # Same length, the one with earlier index wins (we don't update)\n        \n        ans.append(best_index)\n    \n    return ans\n```",
