      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    L = list(map(int, data[2:2+n]))\n    \n    def can_fit(width):\n        lines = 1\n        current_line_width = 0\n        \n        for i in range(n):\n            word_width = L[i]\n            # If first word in line\n            if current_line_width == 0:\n                if word_width > width:\n                    return False\n                current_line_width = word_width\n            else:\n                # Need a space (1) + word\n                if current_line_width + 1 + word_width > width:\n                    lines += 1\n                    current_line_width = word_width\n                    if lines > m:\n                        return False\n                else:\n                    current_line_width += 1 + word_width\n        \n        return True\n    \n    # Binary search on the answer\n    left = max(L)  # At least as wide as the longest word\n    right = sum(L) + (n - 1)  # Worst case: all words in one line with spaces\n    \n    while left < right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if can_fit(mid):\n            right = mid\n        else:\n            left = mid + 1\n    \n    print(left)\n\nsolve()\n```",
