    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef largestPerimeter(nums):\n    nums.sort()\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # Start with the largest possible polygon (using all sides)\n    # and work backwards to find the first valid polygon\n    total_sum = sum(nums)\n    \n    # Remove the largest elements one by one until we find a valid polygon\n    for i in range(n - 1, 1, -1):\n        # If the sum of all smaller sides is greater than the largest side\n        if total_sum - nums[i] > nums[i]:\n            return total_sum\n        \n        # Otherwise, remove the largest side and continue\n        total_sum -= nums[i]\n    \n    # If we've checked all possible combinations and none work\n    return -1\n```",
