    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findKthSmallestAmount(coins, k):\n    import heapq\n    \n    # Use a min heap to efficiently find the kth smallest amount\n    heap = []\n    \n    # For each coin, we'll keep track of the next multiple to consider\n    # Store (next_amount, coin_value, next_multiple_index)\n    for coin in coins:\n        heapq.heappush(heap, (coin, coin, 1))\n    \n    # Remove duplicates and find kth smallest\n    result = 0\n    seen = set()\n    \n    for i in range(k):\n        # Get the smallest amount\n        amount, coin, multiple = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        \n        # Skip if we've seen this amount before\n        while amount in seen:\n            amount = coin * (multiple + 1)\n            multiple += 1\n            heapq.heappush(heap, (amount, coin, multiple))\n            if heap:\n                amount, coin, multiple = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        \n        # Mark as seen\n        seen.add(amount)\n        result = amount\n        \n        # Add next multiple of this coin to heap\n        next_amount = coin * (multiple + 1)\n        heapq.heappush(heap, (next_amount, coin, multiple + 1))\n    \n    return result\n```",
