      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longestSemiRepetitiveSubstring(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the length of the longest semi-repetitive substring.\n    A semi-repetitive string has at most one consecutive pair of the same digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    max_length = 1\n    \n    # Check all possible substrings\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            # Extract substring from i to j (inclusive)\n            substring = s[i:j+1]\n            length = j - i + 1\n            \n            # Count consecutive pairs in the substring\n            consecutive_pairs = 0\n            for k in range(len(substring) - 1):\n                if substring[k] == substring[k + 1]:\n                    consecutive_pairs += 1\n            \n            # If at most one consecutive pair, it's semi-repetitive\n            if consecutive_pairs <= 1:\n                max_length = max(max_length, length)\n    \n    return max_length\n```",
