      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minDeletionsForKSpecial(word, k):\n    # Count frequency of each character\n    freq = {}\n    for char in word:\n        freq[char] = freq.get(char, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Get all frequencies and sort them\n    frequencies = sorted(freq.values())\n    \n    min_deletions = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try each possible target frequency range\n    for i in range(len(frequencies)):\n        target_min = frequencies[i]\n        target_max = target_min + k\n        \n        deletions = 0\n        valid = True\n        \n        for freq_val in frequencies:\n            if freq_val < target_min:\n                # Need to delete all occurrences of this character\n                deletions += freq_val\n            elif freq_val > target_max:\n                # Need to delete excess occurrences\n                deletions += freq_val - target_max\n            # If freq_val is between target_min and target_max, no deletions needed\n        \n        min_deletions = min(min_deletions, deletions)\n    \n    # Also try cases where we can set target range based on higher frequencies\n    for i in range(len(frequencies)):\n        target_max = frequencies[i]\n        target_min = max(1, target_max - k)  # Minimum frequency is 1 if character exists\n        \n        deletions = 0\n        for freq_val in frequencies:\n            if freq_val < target_min:\n                deletions += freq_val\n            elif freq_val > target_max:\n                deletions += freq_val - target_max\n        \n        min_deletions = min(min_deletions, deletions)\n    \n    return min_deletions\n```",
