      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom itertools import permutations\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    H, W = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    \n    A = []\n    for _ in range(H):\n        A.append(list(map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())))\n    \n    B = []\n    for _ in range(H):\n        B.append(list(map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())))\n    \n    # If A is already equal to B\n    if A == B:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    # Check if it's possible: sort all elements and compare\n    flat_A = sorted([A[i][j] for i in range(H) for j in range(W)])\n    flat_B = sorted([B[i][j] for i in range(H) for j in range(W)])\n    \n    if flat_A != flat_B:\n        print(-1)\n        return\n    \n    # Since H, W <= 5, we can try all possible row and column permutations\n    # We need to find the minimum number of adjacent swaps to transform A to B\n    \n    min_operations = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try all row permutations\n    for row_perm in permutations(range(H)):\n        # Try all column permutations\n        for col_perm in permutations(range(W)):\n            # Create transformed grid A based on these permutations\n            transformed = [[0] * W for _ in range(H)]\n            for i in range(H):\n                for j in range(W):\n                    transformed[i][j] = A[row_perm.index(i)][col_perm.index(j)]\n            \n            # Check if this transformed grid matches B\n            if transformed == B:\n                # Calculate minimum adjacent swaps for row permutation\n                row_swaps = 0\n                row_arr = list(row_perm)\n                # Bubble sort to count adjacent swaps\n                for i in range(H):\n                    for j in range(H - 1):\n                        if row_arr[j] > row_arr[j + 1]:\n                            row_arr[j], row_arr[j + 1] = row_arr[j + 1], row_arr[j]\n                            row_swaps += 1\n                \n                # Calculate minimum adjacent swaps for column permutation\n                col_swaps = 0\n                col_arr = list(col_perm)\n                for i in range(W):\n                    for j in range(W - 1):\n                        if col_arr[j] > col_arr[j + 1]:\n                            col_arr[j], col_arr[j + 1] = col_arr[j + 1], col_arr[j]\n                            col_swaps += 1\n                \n                min_operations = min(min_operations, row_swaps + col_swaps)\n    \n    if min_operations == float('inf'):\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(min_operations)\n\nsolve()\n```",
