      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n    points = []\n    \n    for _ in range(N):\n        x, y = map(int, input().split())\n        points.append((x, y))\n    \n    # For each point, find the farthest point\n    for i in range(N):\n        max_distance = -1\n        farthest_id = -1\n        \n        for j in range(N):\n            if i != j:  # Don't compare a point with itself\n                # Calculate Euclidean distance\n                x1, y1 = points[i]\n                x2, y2 = points[j]\n                distance = math.sqrt((x1 - x2)**2 + (y1 - y2)**2)\n                \n                # If this point is farther, or same distance but smaller ID\n                if distance > max_distance or (distance == max_distance and j + 1 < farthest_id):\n                    max_distance = distance\n                    farthest_id = j + 1  # ID is 1-indexed\n        \n        print(farthest_id)\n\nsolve()\n```",
