      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n    \n    # Read the adjacency matrix\n    adjacency_matrix = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        row = list(map(int, input().split()))\n        adjacency_matrix.append(row)\n    \n    # For each vertex i, find all vertices directly connected to it\n    for i in range(N):\n        connected_vertices = []\n        for j in range(N):\n            if adjacency_matrix[i][j] == 1:\n                connected_vertices.append(j + 1)  # Convert to 1-based indexing\n        \n        # Print the connected vertices in ascending order (they're already in order by j)\n        print(' '.join(map(str, connected_vertices)))\n\nsolve()\n```",
