      "generated_answer": "I'll solve this step-by-step.\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\n1. We need to find subarrays that, when removed, make the remaining array strictly increasing\n2. A strictly increasing array means each element is greater than the previous one\n3. The remaining array after removal must be strictly increasing (or empty)\n4. We need to count all possible subarrays that satisfy this condition\n\n## Key Insights\n\n1. After removing a subarray, we have elements from the beginning and end of the original array\n2. For the remaining array to be strictly increasing:\n   - The prefix (elements before the removed subarray) must be strictly increasing\n   - The suffix (elements after the removed subarray) must be strictly increasing\n   - If both prefix and suffix exist, the last element of prefix must be < first element of suffix\n\n## Strategy\n\n1. Try all possible subarrays (defined by start and end indices)\n2. For each subarray removal, check if the remaining elements form a strictly increasing sequence\n3. Count valid cases\n\n## Step-by-Step Solution\n\nLet me trace through Example 2: `nums = [6,5,7,8]`\n- Remove [5]: remaining [6,7,8] → strictly increasing ✓\n- Remove [6]: remaining [5,7,8] → strictly increasing ✓  \n- Remove [5,7]: remaining [6,8] → 6 < 8, strictly increasing ✓\n- Remove [6,5]: remaining [7,8] → 7 < 8, strictly increasing ✓\n- Remove [5,7,8]: remaining [6] → single element, strictly increasing ✓\n- Remove [6,5,7]: remaining [8] → single element, strictly increasing ✓\n- Remove [6,5,7,8]: remaining [] → empty array, considered strictly increasing ✓\n\n## Implementation\n\n```python\ndef incremovableSubarrayCount(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    count = 0\n    \n    # Try all possible subarrays (start, end) inclusive\n    for start in range(n):\n        for end in range(start, n):\n            # Create the remaining array after removing subarray [start:end+1]\n            remaining = []\n            \n            # Add elements before the removed subarray\n            for i in range(start):\n                remaining.append(nums[i])\n            \n            # Add elements after the removed subarray\n            for i in range(end + 1, n):\n                remaining.append(nums[i])\n            \n            # Check if remaining array is strictly increasing\n            is_strictly_increasing = True\n            \n            # Empty array or single element is considered strictly increasing\n            if len(remaining) <= 1:\n                is_strictly_increasing = True\n            else:\n                # Check each adjacent pair\n                for i in range(1, len(remaining)):\n                    if remaining[i] <= remaining[i-1]:\n                        is_strictly_increasing = False\n                        break\n            \n            if is_strictly_increasing:\n                count += 1\n    \n    return count\n```",
