    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumString(a: str, b: str, c: str) -> str:\n    def merge(s1, s2):\n        # Find the shortest string that contains both s1 and s2\n        if s2 in s1:\n            return s1\n        # Try to overlap s2 with the end of s1\n        for i in range(len(s1) + 1):\n            if s1[i:] == s2[:len(s1) - i]:\n                return s1 + s2[len(s1) - i:]\n        return s1 + s2\n    \n    def merge_three(s1, s2, s3):\n        # Merge three strings by trying different merge orders\n        result = []\n        # Try all permutations of the three strings\n        candidates = [\n            merge(merge(s1, s2), s3),\n            merge(merge(s1, s3), s2),\n            merge(merge(s2, s1), s3),\n            merge(merge(s2, s3, s1, s1),\n            merge(merge(s3, s2), s1),\n            merge(merge(s2, s3), s1)\n        ]\n        \n        # Filter out None values and find the minimum\n        valid_candidates = [cand for cand in candidates if cand]\n        \n        if not valid_candidates:\n            return \"\"\n            \n        # Find the shortest length\n        min_length = min(len(cand) for cand in valid_candidates)\n        # Among those with minimum length, find lexicographically smallest\n        result = min(cand for cand in valid_candidates if len(cand) == min_length)\n        \n        return result\n    \n    # Try all possible orderings of the three strings\n    strings = [a, b, c]\n    candidates = []\n    \n    # Generate all permutations manually\n    permutations = [\n        (strings[0], strings[1], strings[2]),\n        (strings[0], strings[2], strings[1]),\n        (strings[1], strings[0], strings[2]),\n        (strings[1], strings[2], strings[0]),\n        (strings[2], strings[0], strings[1]),\n        (strings[2], strings[1], strings[0])\n    ]\n    \n    for s1, s2, s3 in permutations:\n        # First merge s1 and s2, then merge with s3\n        temp = merge(s1, s2)\n        final = merge(temp, s3)\n        candidates.append(final)\n    \n    # Find the answer - shortest length, then lexicographically smallest\n    min_length = min(len(candidate) for candidate in candidates)\n    candidates = [c for c in candidates if len(c) == min_length]\n    \n    return min(candidates)\n```",
