      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef solve():\n    n = int(input())\n    slimes = {}\n    for _ in range(n):\n        s, c = map(int, input().split())\n        slimes[s] = c\n    \n    # Use a dictionary to store count of slimes for each size\n    count = defaultdict(int)\n    for s, c in slimes.items():\n        count[s] = c\n    \n    # Process from smallest to largest size\n    # The idea is to process each size and carry over the odd part to the next level\n    sizes = sorted(count.keys())\n    \n    total_slimes = 0\n    \n    for size in sizes:\n        cnt = count[size]\n        # Number of times we can combine slimes of this size (each combination reduces count by 2)\n        # Add the remainder to total since they can't be combined anymore at this level\n        total_slimes += cnt % 2\n        \n        # Carry over the combinations to the next size (size * 2)\n        next_count = cnt // 2\n        if next_count > 0:\n            count[size * 2] += next_count\n    \n    # We need to process higher levels that were created by combination\n    # Get all non-zero counts in order\n    all_sizes = sorted([k for k, v in count.items() if v > 0])\n    \n    # Recalculate total - we'll just check all existing sizes\n    result = 0\n    for size in all_sizes:\n        if count[size] > 0:\n            result += count[size] % 2\n            # Propagate combinations to next level\n            next_level = count[size] // 2\n            if next_level > 0:\n                count[size * 2] += next_level\n    \n    # Need to continue until no more combinations can be made\n    # Use a while loop to process all levels\n    processed = set()\n    while True:\n        new_sizes = sorted([k for k, v in count.items() if v > 0 and k not in processed])\n        if not new_sizes:\n            break\n            \n        changed = False\n        for size in new_sizes:\n            if count[size] == 0:\n                continue\n            cnt = count[size]\n            # Add odd part to result\n            if cnt % 2 == 1:\n                result -= 1  # subtract the previous contribution\n                result += 1  # this will be the same, but we're recalculating\n                \n            # Carry over to next level\n            next_count = cnt // 2\n            if next_count > 0:\n                count[size * 2] += next_count\n                changed = True\n            \n            count[size] = cnt % 2\n            processed.add(size)\n            \n        if not changed:\n            break\n    \n    # Final count - sum all remaining non-zero counts\n    final_result = 0\n    for k, v in count.items():\n        if v > 0:\n            final_result += v % 2  # only the odd part remains\n    \n    # The above approach is complex, let's use a simpler simulation\n    # Clear and start over with simpler approach\n    count = defaultdict(int)\n    for s, c in slimes.items():\n        count[s] = c\n    \n    # Use a while loop to simulate the process\n    while True:\n        # Find the smallest size that has at least 2 slimes\n        sizes = sorted([k for k, v in count.items() if v >= 2])\n        if not sizes:\n            break\n        \n        # Take the smallest size with at least 2 slimes\n        size = sizes[0]\n        if count[size] < 2:\n            continue\n            \n        # Combine two slimes of this size\n        combine_count = count[size] // 2\n        count[size] -= combine_count * 2\n        count[size * 2] += combine_count\n    \n    # Count total remaining slimes\n    result = sum(v for v in count.values() if v > 0)\n    print(result)\n\n# Actually, let me use a cleaner, correct approach:\ndef solve():\n    n = int(input())\n    slimes = {}\n    for _ in range(n):\n        s, c = map(int, input().split())\n        slimes[s] = c\n    \n    # Use a dictionary for counts\n    count = defaultdict(int)\n    for s, c in slimes.items():\n        count[s] = c\n    \n    # We'll process recursively from smallest to largest\n    # But easier: simulate until no more combinations\n    processed = False\n    \n    while True:\n        # Get current non-zero counts in sorted order\n        sizes = sorted([k for k, v in count.items() if v > 0])\n        found_combination = False\n        \n        for size in sizes:\n            if count[size] >= 2:\n                # Can combine\n                combine_pairs = count[size] // 2\n                count[size] -= combine_pairs * 2\n                count[size * 2] += combine_pairs\n                found_combination = True\n                break\n        \n        if not found_combination:\n            break\n    \n    # Sum up remaining slimes\n    result = sum(count[size] for size in count if count[size] > 0)\n    print(result)\n\nsolve()\n```",
