      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    \n    medicines = []\n    index = 2\n    for _ in range(n):\n        a = int(data[index])\n        b = int(data[index + 1])\n        index += 2\n        medicines.append((a, b))\n    \n    # For each medicine, it contributes b pills from day 1 to day a (inclusive)\n    # We need to find the first day when the total pills <= k\n    \n    # We can binary search on the day number\n    def pills_on_day(day):\n        total = 0\n        for a, b in medicines:\n            if day <= a:  # if the day is within the medicine's duration\n                total += b\n            # if day > a, then this medicine is no longer taken\n        return total\n    \n    # Edge case: if we already have <= k on day 1\n    if pills_on_day(1) <= k:\n        print(1)\n        return\n    \n    # Binary search on the answer\n    left = 1\n    # Maximum possible day: the maximum duration of any medicine + 1 (just in case)\n    max_day = max(a for a, b in medicines) + 1\n    \n    right = max_day\n    result = right\n    \n    while left <= right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        total_pills = pills_on_day(mid)\n        \n        if total_pills <= k:\n            result = mid\n            right = mid - 1\n        else:\n            left = mid + 1\n    \n    print(result)\n\nsolve()\n```",
