from bus stop 1 at time 15 and arrive at bus stop 2 at time 19.\n- Take the bus departing from bus stop 2 at time 24 and arrive at bus stop 3 at time 30.\n- Take the bus departing from bus stop 3 at time 30 and arrive at bus stop 4 at time 31.\n- Walk from bus stop 4 and arrive at Aoki's house at time 34.\n\nFor the second query, Takahashi can move as follows and arrive at Aoki's house at time 22.\n\n- Leave his house at time 0.\n- Walk from his house and arrive at bus stop 1 at time 2.\n- Take the bus departing from bus stop 1 at time 5 and arrive at bus stop 2 at time 9.\n- Take the bus departing from bus stop 2 at time 12 and arrive at bus stop 3 at time 18.\n- Take the bus departing from bus stop 3 at time 18 and arrive at bus stop 4 at time 19.\n- Walk from bus stop 4 and arrive at Aoki's house at time 22.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We need to simulate the bus schedule for Takahashi’s journey from his house to Aoki’s house, given that he can only catch buses that depart at multiples of `P_i` from bus stop `i`.\n\n### Strategy:\n1. **Walk to first bus stop**: Takes `X` time, so arrival at stop 1 is `start_time + X`.\n2. **For each bus stop `i` (from 1 to N-1)**:\n   - Wait at stop `i` until the next (or current) multiple of `P_i` that is ≥ current time.\n   - Then ride the bus which takes `T_i` time to reach stop `i+1`.\n3. **After reaching stop `N`**, walk to Aoki's house: add `Y` time.\n\nWe’ll process each query by simulating this forward journey.\n\nBecause `P_i ≤ 8`, computing the next multiple of `P_i` is fast.\n\n---\n\n### Python Implementation\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    # Parse first line\n    N = int(data[0])\n    X = int(data[1])\n    Y = int(data[2])\n    \n    buses = []\n    index = 3\n    for i in range(N - 1):\n        P = int(data[index])\n        T = int(data[index + 1])\n        index += 2\n        buses.append((P, T))\n    \n    Q = int(data[index])\n    index += 1\n    queries = [int(data[index + i]) for i in range(Q)]\n    \n    # Precompute nothing? Just simulate each query.\n    results = []\n    for q in queries:\n        time = q + X  # arrive at bus stop 1\n        \n        # Ride each bus from stop 1 to stop N-1\n        for P, T in buses:\n            # Wait until the next departure time (multiple of P >= current time)\n            if time % P != 0:\n                time += P - (time % P)\n            # Take the bus\n            time += T\n        \n        # Walk from stop N to Aoki's house\n        time += Y\n        results.append(str(time))\n    \n    print(\"\\n\".join(results))\n\nsolve()\n```\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of Key Part:\n- `time % P != 0`: means we have to wait.\n- `time += P - (time % P)`: rounds `time` up to the next multiple of `P`.\n\nThis correctly handles the bus departure times.\n\n---\n\n### Sample Verification:\n- Query `q=0`:\n  - `time = 0 + 2 = 2` (arrive at stop 1)\n  - Bus 1: `P=5`, wait to 5, then `5+4=9`\n  - Bus 2: `P=6`, wait to 12, then `12+6=18`\n  - Bus 3: `P=3`, 18%3==0 → take at 18, arrive at 18+1=19\n  - Walk: 19+3 = 22 → correct.\n\nMatches sample.\n\n---\n\n### Call the function\nWe already call `solve()` at the end.\n\n✅ This code reads stdin, processes all queries, and prints the answers.",
