      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef count_substrings(s, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Count the total number of substrings of s that start and end with character c.\n    \n    Args:\n        s (str): Input string\n        c (str): Target character\n    \n    Returns:\n        int: Number of substrings that start and end with c\n    \"\"\"\n    # Count occurrences of character c in the string\n    count = 0\n    for char in s:\n        if char == c:\n            count += 1\n    \n    # If there are n occurrences of character c,\n    # the number of ways to choose 2 positions (start and end) is n*(n+1)/2\n    # This is because each pair of occurrences (including same position for length 1 substrings)\n    # forms a valid substring that starts and ends with c\n    return count * (count + 1) // 2\n```",
