    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_420",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nYou are given a tree with N vertices. The vertices are numbered 1 to N, and the i-th edge connects vertices A_i and B_i.\nYou are also given a sequence of positive integers C = (C_1, C_2, \\ldots ,C_N) of length N. Let d(a, b) be the number of edges between vertices a and b, and for x = 1, 2, \\ldots, N, let \\displaystyle f(x) = \\sum_{{i=1}}^{{N}} (C_i \\times d(x, i)). Find \\displaystyle \\min_{{1 \\leq v \\leq N}} f(v).\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\nA_1 B_1\nA_2 B_2\n\\vdots\nA_{{N - 1}} B_{{N - 1}}\nC_1 C_2 \\cdots C_N\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer in one line.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N \\leq 10^5\n- 1 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq N\n- The given graph is a tree.\n- 1 \\leq C_i \\leq 10^9\n\nSample Input 1\n\n4\n1 2\n1 3\n2 4\n1 1 1 2\n\nSample Output 1\n\n5\n\nFor example, consider calculating f(1). We have d(1, 1) = 0, d(1, 2) = 1, d(1, 3) = 1, d(1, 4) = 2.\nThus, f(1) = 0 \\times 1 + 1 \\times 1 + 1 \\times 1 + 2 \\times 2 = 6.\nSimilarly, f(2) = 5, f(3) = 9, f(4) = 6. Since f(2) is the minimum, print 5.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n2\n2 1\n1 1000000000\n\nSample Output 2\n\n1\n\nf(2) = 1, which is the minimum.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n7\n7 3\n2 5\n2 4\n3 1\n3 6\n2 1\n2 7 6 9 3 4 6\n\nSample Output 3\n\n56",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict, deque\n\ndef solve():\n    N = int(sys.stdin.readline())\n    \n    # Build adjacency list\n    graph = defaultdict(list)\n    for _ in range(N - 1):\n        a, b = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n        graph[a].append(b)\n        graph[b].append(a)\n    \n    # Read weights\n    C = list(map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split()))\n    # Create 1-indexed C (C[i] corresponds to vertex i)\n    C = [0] + C  # Now C[1] is the weight of vertex 1, etc.\n    \n    if N == 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    # First, pick an arbitrary root (say 1) and compute:\n    # 1. The total cost f(1) \n    # 2. Subtree weights (sum of C[i] for each subtree)\n    \n    parent = [-1] * (N + 1)\n    subtree_weight = [0] * (N + 1)  # sum of C[i] in the subtree rooted at i\n    order = []\n    \n    # DFS to set up parent and traversal order\n    stack = [1]\n    while stack:\n        u = stack.pop()\n        order.append(u)\n        for v in graph[u]:\n            if v != parent[u]:\n                parent[v] = u\n                stack.append(v)\n    \n    # Compute subtree weights (process nodes in reverse order)\n    for u in reversed(order):\n        subtree_weight[u] = C[u]\n        for v in graph[u]:\n            if v != parent[u]:\n                subtree_weight[u] += subtree_weight[v]\n    \n    # Compute f(1) using BFS\n    visited = [False] * (N + 1)\n    dist = [0] * (N + 1)\n    queue = deque([1])\n    visited[1] = True\n    f_root = 0\n    \n    while queue:\n        u = queue.popleft()\n        f_root += dist[u] * C[u]\n        for v in graph[u]:\n            if not visited[v]:\n                visited[v] = True\n                dist[v] = dist[u] + 1\n                queue.append(v)\n    \n    # If we move from parent to child, how does f change?\n    # When moving from u to v (where v is child of u):\n    # - All nodes in subtree of v get 1 closer: gain = subtree_weight[v]\n    # - All other nodes (including u's part) get 1 farther: loss = (total_weight - subtree_weight[v])\n    # So delta = -subtree_weight[v] + (total_weight - subtree_weight[v]) = total_weight - 2 * subtree_weight[v]\n    \n    total_weight = subtree_weight[1]\n    min_f = f_root\n    \n    # Use DFS to compute f(v) for all nodes using the re-rooting technique\n    stack = [(1, f_root)]\n    while stack:\n        u, f_u = stack.pop()\n        min_f = min(min_f, f_u)\n        \n        for v in graph[u]:\n            if v == parent[u]:\n                continue\n            # Move from u to v\n            f_v = f_u + total_weight - 2 * subtree_weight[v]\n            stack.append((v, f_v))\n    \n    print(min_f)\n\nsolve()\n```",
