    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to count the number of strings of length n that can be rearranged to contain \"leet\" as a substring.\n\nFor a string to be \"good\", when rearranged it must contain \"leet\". This means the string must have:\n- At least 1 'l'\n- At least 2 'e's  \n- At least 1 't'\n\nLet me use the inclusion-exclusion principle:\n1. Total possible strings: 26^n\n2. Subtract strings missing at least one required letter\n3. Add back strings missing at least two required letters (over-subtracted)\n4. Subtract strings missing at least three required letters\n\nLet:\n- A = strings without 'l'\n- B = strings without at least 2 'e's (i.e., 0 or 1 'e')\n- C = strings without 't'\n\nWe want: Total - (A ∪ B ∪ C) = Total - (|A| + |B| + |C| - |A∩B| - |A∩C| - |B∩C| + |A∩B∩C|)\n\nWhere:\n- Total = 26^n\n- |A| = 25^n (no 'l')\n- |C| = 25^n (no 't') \n- |B| = strings with 0 'e's + strings with 1 'e' = 25^n + n×25^(n-1)\n- |A∩B| = no 'l' and (0 or 1 'e') = 24^n + n×24^(n-1)\n- |A∩C| = no 'l' and no 't' = 24^n\n- |B∩C| = no 't' and (0 or 1 'e') = 24^n + n×24^(n-1)\n- |A∩B∩C| = no 'l', no 't', and (0 or 1 'e') = 23^n + n×23^(n-1)\n\n```python\ndef countGoodStrings(n: int) -> int:\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    \n    # Total strings\n    total = pow(26, n, MOD)\n    \n    # Strings without 'l'\n    without_l = pow(25, n, MOD)\n    \n    # Strings without 't'\n    without_t = pow(25, n, MOD)\n    \n    # Strings with 0 or 1 'e'\n    without_2e = (pow(25, n, MOD) + n * pow(25, n-1, MOD)) % MOD\n    \n    # Strings without 'l' and with 0 or 1 'e'\n    without_l_and_2e = (pow(24, n, MOD) + n * pow(24, n-1, MOD)) % MOD\n    \n    # Strings without 'l' and without 't'\n    without_l_and_t = pow(24, n, MOD)\n    \n    # Strings without 't' and with 0 or 1 'e'\n    without_t_and_2e = (pow(24, n, MOD) + n * pow(24, n-1, MOD)) % MOD\n    \n    # Strings without 'l', without 't', and with 0 or 1 'e'\n    without_l_t_and_2e = (pow(23, n, MOD) + n * pow(23, n-1, MOD)) % MOD\n    \n    # Apply inclusion-exclusion principle\n    result = (total - without_l - without_t - without_2e + without_l_and_2e + without_l_and_t + without_t_and_2e - without_l_t_and_2e) % MOD\n    \n    return result\n```",
