      "generated_answer": "I need to create a function that finds the punishment number for a given positive integer n.\n\nLet me break down the problem:\n1. For each integer i from 1 to n, I need to check if the square of i can be partitioned into contiguous substrings such that the sum of these substrings equals i.\n2. If the condition is met, I add i² to the result.\n3. Return the sum of all such i² values.\n\nTo check if a number can be partitioned as required, I'll use a recursive approach to try all possible ways to split the string representation of i².\n\n```python\ndef punishmentNumber(n):\n    def can_partition(s, target, start):\n        if start == len(s):\n            return target == 0\n        \n        for i in range(start + 1, len(s) + 1):\n            num = int(s[start:i])\n            if num <= target and can_partition(s, target - num, i):\n                return True\n        return False\n    \n    total = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        square_str = str(square)\n        if can_partition(square_str, i, 0):\n            total += square\n    \n    return total\n```",
