      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n    \n    people = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        C_i = int(input())\n        bets = list(map(int, input().split()))\n        people.append((i + 1, C_i, set(bets)))  # (person number, number of bets, set of bets)\n    \n    X = int(input())\n    \n    # Find all people who bet on X\n    betting_people = []\n    for person_num, num_bets, bet_set in people:\n        if X in bet_set:\n            betting_people.append((person_num, num_bets))\n    \n    # If no one bet on X, output 0 and empty line\n    if not betting_people:\n        print(0)\n        print()\n        return\n    \n    # Find the minimum number of bets among those who bet on X\n    min_bets = min(num_bets for _, num_bets in betting_people)\n    \n    # Find all people who bet on X and have the minimum number of bets\n    winners = [person_num for person_num, num_bets in betting_people if num_bets == min_bets]\n    winners.sort()\n    \n    # Output\n    print(len(winners))\n    if winners:\n        print(*winners)\n    else:\n        print()\n\nsolve()\n```",
