      "generated_answer": "I need to solve the problem of counting complete substrings.\n\nA complete substring must:\n1. Have each character occur exactly k times\n2. Have adjacent characters with alphabet position difference of at most 2\n\nThe key insight is that if each character appears exactly k times, the length of the substring must be (number of unique characters) × k.\n\nI'll iterate through all possible starting positions and for each position, check substrings of length k, 2k, 3k, ..., up to 26k (since there are at most 26 unique letters).\n\n```python\ndef countCompleteSubstrings(word, k):\n    def isValidSubstring(s):\n        # Check if each character occurs exactly k times\n        char_count = {}\n        for char in s:\n            char_count[char] = char_count.get(char, 0) + 1\n        \n        # Check if each character occurs exactly k times\n        for count in char_count.values():\n            if count != k:\n                return False\n        \n        # Check if difference between adjacent characters is at most 2\n        for i in range(len(s) - 1):\n            diff = abs(ord(s[i]) - ord(s[i + 1]))\n            if diff > 2:\n                return False\n        \n        return True\n    \n    n = len(word)\n    count = 0\n    \n    # Check all possible starting positions\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Check substrings of length k, 2k, 3k, ..., up to 26k\n        # (at most 26 unique characters)\n        for num_unique in range(1, 27):\n            length = num_unique * k\n            j = i + length\n            \n            # If substring would go out of bounds, break\n            if j > n:\n                break\n                \n            substring = word[i:j]\n            \n            # Check if valid\n            if isValidSubstring(substring):\n                count += 1\n    \n    return count\n```",
