      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    from itertools import permutations\n    \n    # Read input\n    lines = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    if not lines:\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n        \n    N, H, W = map(int, lines[0].split())\n    tiles = []\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        a, b = map(int, lines[i].split())\n        # Store both orientations of the tile\n        tiles.append((a, b))\n        tiles.append((b, a))\n    \n    # Total cells in the grid\n    total_cells = H * W\n    grid = [[0] * W for _ in range(H)]  # 0 means empty, 1 means filled\n    \n    def can_place(r, c, h, w):\n        \"\"\"Check if a tile of size h x w can be placed at position (r, c)\"\"\"\n        if r + h > H or c + w > W:\n            return False\n        for i in range(r, r + h):\n            for j in range(c, j + w):\n                if grid[i][j] == 1:\n                    return False\n        return True\n    \n    def place_tile(r, c, h, w, value):\n        \"\"\"Place or remove a tile of size h x w at position (r, c)\"\"\"\n        for i in range(r, r + h):\n            for j in range(c, c + w):\n                grid[i][j] = value\n    \n    def backtrack(idx):\n        \"\"\"Try to fill the grid starting from cell idx\"\"\"\n        if idx == total_cells:\n            return True\n            \n        r, c = idx // W, idx % W\n        if grid[r][c] == 1:\n            return backtrack(idx + 1)\n        \n        # Try each tile\n        for i in range(len(tiles)):\n            h, w = tiles[i]\n            \n            # Skip if tile is too big\n            if r + h > H or c + w > W:\n                continue\n                \n            # Check if we can place this tile\n            can_place_tile = True\n            for dr in range(h):\n                for dc in range(w):\n                    if grid[r + dr][c + dc] == 1:\n                        can_place_tile = False\n                        break\n                if not can_place_tile:\n                    break\n                    \n            if can_place_tile:\n                # Place the tile\n                place_tile(r, c, h, w, 1)\n                \n                # Recurse\n                if backtrack(idx + 1):\n                    return True\n                    \n                # Remove the tile (backtrack)\n                place_tile(r, c, h, w, 0)\n                \n        return False\n    \n    # Use recursive backtracking to try all combinations\n    # But first check if total area of tiles >= grid area\n    max_area = sum(max(a, b) * min(a, b) for a, b in [tiles[i] for i in range(0, len(tiles), 2)])\n    \n    if max_area < total_cells:\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n        \n    # Try to fill the grid\n    if backtrack(0):\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
