    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumBeautifulSubstrings(s):\n    # Precompute all powers of 5 in binary that could fit in a string of length <= 15\n    powers_of_5_binary = []\n    power = 1\n    while True:\n        binary = bin(power)[2:]  # Convert to binary without '0b' prefix\n        if len(binary) > 15:\n            break\n        powers_of_5_binary.append(binary)\n        power *= 5\n    \n    # Sort by length (descending) for efficiency in matching\n    powers_of_5_binary.sort(key=lambda x: len(x), reverse=True)\n    \n    def can_partition(string, start, memo):\n        if start == len(string):\n            return 0\n        \n        if start in memo:\n            return memo[start]\n        \n        # If current character is '0', we cannot form a beautiful substring (due to leading zero)\n        if string[start] == '0':\n            memo[start] = float('inf')\n            return float('inf')\n        \n        min_partitions = float('inf')\n        \n        # Try all possible substrings starting from current position\n        for end in range(start + 1, len(string) + 1):\n            substring = string[start:end]\n            # Check if this substring is a power of 5 in binary and has no leading zeros\n            if substring in powers_of_5_binary:\n                result = can_partition(string, end, memo)\n                if result != float('inf'):\n                    min_partitions = min(min_partitions, 1 + result)\n        \n        memo[start] = min_partitions\n        return min_partitions\n    \n    memo = {}\n    result = can_partition(s, 0, memo)\n    \n    return result if result != float('inf') else -1\n```",
