      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef canSortArray(nums):\n    def count_set_bits(n):\n        return bin(n).count('1')\n    \n    # Group elements by their set bit count\n    groups = []\n    current_group = []\n    current_bit_count = count_set_bits(nums[0])\n    \n    for num in nums:\n        bit_count = count_set_bits(num)\n        if bit_count == current_bit_count:\n            current_group.append(num)\n        else:\n            if current_group:\n                groups.append(current_group)\n            current_group = [num]\n            current_bit_count = bit_count\n    \n    # Don't forget the last group\n    if current_group:\n        groups.append(current_group)\n    \n    # For each group, check if its elements can be arranged to match sorted order\n    sorted_nums = sorted(nums)\n    sorted_groups = []\n    current_sorted_group = []\n    current_bit_count = count_set_bits(sorted_nums[0])\n    \n    for num in sorted_nums:\n        bit_count = count_set_bits(num)\n        if bit_count == current_bit_count:\n            current_sorted_group.append(num)\n        else:\n            if current_sorted_group:\n                sorted_groups.append(current_sorted_group)\n            current_sorted_group = [num]\n            current_bit_count = bit_count\n    \n    # Don't forget the last group\n    if current_sorted_group:\n        sorted_groups.append(current_sorted_group)\n    \n    # Check if the group structures are compatible\n    if len(groups) != len(sorted_groups):\n        return False\n    \n    # Check if each group contains the same elements as the corresponding sorted group\n    for i in range(len(groups)):\n        if sorted(groups[i]) != sorted_groups[i]:\n            return False\n    \n    return True\n```",
