    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n    A = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    \n    # We need to find the minimum possible current number of passengers\n    # Let x be the initial number of passengers\n    # After each stop i, the number of passengers is: x + prefix_sum[i]\n    # All values must be >= 0\n    \n    prefix_sum = 0\n    min_prefix_sum = 0  # This tracks the minimum prefix sum\n    \n    for i in range(N):\n        prefix_sum += A[i]\n        min_prefix_sum = min(min_prefix_sum, prefix_sum)\n    \n    # The initial number of passengers must be at least -min_prefix_sum\n    # So the current number of passengers is: initial + total_sum\n    # = (-min_prefix_sum) + prefix_sum (after all stops)\n    initial_needed = max(0, -min_prefix_sum)\n    current_passengers = initial_needed + prefix_sum\n    \n    print(current_passengers)\n\nsolve()\n```",
