    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimum_operations(x: int, y: int) -> int:\n    from collections import deque\n    \n    if x == y:\n        return 0\n    \n    # BFS to find minimum operations\n    queue = deque([(x, 0)])  # (current_value, operations_count)\n    visited = {x}\n    \n    while queue:\n        current, ops = queue.popleft()\n        \n        # Try all possible operations\n        next_states = []\n        \n        # Operation 1: Divide by 11 if multiple of 11\n        if current % 11 == 0:\n            next_states.append(current // 11)\n        \n        # Operation 2: Divide by 5 if multiple of 5\n        if current % 5 == 0:\n            next_states.append(current // 5)\n        \n        # Operation 3: Decrement by 1\n        next_states.append(current - 1)\n        \n        # Operation 4: Increment by 1\n        next_states.append(current + 1)\n        \n        for next_val in next_states:\n            if next_val == y:\n                return ops + 1\n            \n            if next_val > 0 and next_val not in visited:\n                visited.add(next_val)\n                queue.append((next_val, ops + 1))\n    \n    return -1  # This should not happen given the constraints\n```",
