    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the minimum number of boxes required to hold all the apples.\n\nThe key insights are:\n1. I need to sum all the apples from all packs\n2. I want to use the fewest boxes possible, so I should use the largest capacity boxes first (greedy approach)\n3. I need to count how many boxes are needed to hold the total apple count\n\nHere's my approach:\n1. Calculate the total number of apples\n2. Sort the capacity array in descending order\n3. Greedily select boxes starting from the largest capacity\n4. Keep adding box capacities until I can hold all apples\n5. Return the count of boxes used\n\n```python\ndef minimumBoxes(apple, capacity):\n    total_apples = sum(apple)\n    capacity.sort(reverse=True)\n    \n    boxes_used = 0\n    current_capacity = 0\n    \n    for cap in capacity:\n        if current_capacity >= total_apples:\n            break\n        current_capacity += cap\n        boxes_used += 1\n    \n    return boxes_used\n```",
