ms)\n    count = 0\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        current_max = nums[i]\n        # Look for all positions j >= i where we can end the subarray\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            # Update the maximum in the current subarray\n            if nums[j] > current_max:\n                current_max = nums[j]\n                # If current_max > nums[i], then nums[i] can't be the maximum anymore\n                # So no valid subarray starting at i can extend beyond this point\n                break\n            \n            # If we reach an element equal to nums[i] and current_max is nums[i]\n            # (which means no larger element has been seen and nums[i] is the max)\n            if nums[j] == nums[i] and current_max == nums[i]:\n                count += 1\n    \n    return count\n```",
