    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef getSmallestString(s: str, k: int) -> str:\n    if k == 0:\n        return s\n    \n    result = []\n    remaining_k = k\n    \n    for char in s:\n        if remaining_k == 0:\n            result.append(char)\n            continue\n            \n        # Current character's ASCII value\n        current_ord = ord(char)\n        # 'a' ASCII value\n        a_ord = ord('a')\n        \n        # Distance from current character to 'a' in cyclic manner\n        # Two possible paths: direct or through the cycle\n        direct_distance = current_ord - a_ord\n        cycle_distance = 26 - direct_distance\n        min_distance_to_a = min(direct_distance, cycle_distance)\n        \n        if min_distance_to_a <= remaining_k:\n            # We can change this character to 'a'\n            result.append('a')\n            remaining_k -= min_distance_to_a\n        else:\n            # We can't change to 'a', so we change to the lexicographically smallest\n            # character possible within remaining_k budget\n            if current_ord - remaining_k >= a_ord:\n                # Move backward in alphabet\n                new_char = chr(current_ord - remaining_k)\n            else:\n                # Need to wrap around - calculate position from 'z' backward\n                remaining_after_a = remaining_k - (current_ord - a_ord)\n                new_char = chr(ord('z') - remaining_after_a + 1)\n            \n            result.append(new_char)\n            remaining_k = 0\n    \n    return ''.join(result)\n```",
