    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given two strings s and t of equal length n. You can perform the following operation on the string s:\n\nRemove a suffix of s of length l where 0 < l < n and append it at the start of s.\n\tFor example, let s = 'abcd' then in one operation you can remove the suffix 'cd' and append it in front of s making s = 'cdab'.\n\nYou are also given an integer k. Return the number of ways in which s can be transformed into t in exactly k operations.\nSince the answer can be large, return it modulo 10^9 + 7.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: s = \"abcd\", t = \"cdab\", k = 2\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: \nFirst way:\nIn first operation, choose suffix from index = 3, so resulting s = \"dabc\".\nIn second operation, choose suffix from index = 3, so resulting s = \"cdab\".\n\nSecond way:\nIn first operation, choose suffix from index = 1, so resulting s = \"bcda\".\nIn second operation, choose suffix from index = 1, so resulting s = \"cdab\".\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: s = \"ababab\", t = \"ababab\", k = 1\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: \nFirst way:\nChoose suffix from index = 2, so resulting s = \"ababab\".\n\nSecond way:\nChoose suffix from index = 4, so resulting s = \"ababab\".\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n2 <= s.length <= 5 * 10^5\n1 <= k <= 10^15\ns.length == t.length\ns and t consist of only lowercase English alphabets.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef numberOfWays(s, t, k):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # Find all valid rotation positions where s can become t\n    valid_positions = []\n    doubled_s = s + s\n    for i in range(n):\n        if doubled_s[i:i+n] == t:\n            valid_positions.append(i)\n    \n    if not valid_positions:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Matrix exponentiation approach to solve recurrence\n    # We need to compute dp[k] where:\n    # dp[i][0] = number of ways to reach target position at step i\n    # dp[i][1] = number of ways to reach non-target position at step i\n    \n    # If we're at target position, next move can go to (n-1) non-target positions\n    # If we're at non-target position, next move can go to 1 target position and (n-2) other non-target positions\n    \n    target_count = len(valid_positions)\n    non_target_count = n - target_count\n    \n    # We start at position 0 (original string s)\n    # Check if original s is already t\n    start_at_target = 1 if s == t else 0\n    start_at_non_target = 1 if s != t else 0\n    \n    # For k = 1, handle directly\n    if k == 1:\n        return target_count if s != t else (target_count - 1) % MOD\n    \n    # Use matrix exponentiation to compute result for large k\n    # State transition matrix:\n    # [ways_to_target]   = [0     non_target_count] ^ k [initial_at_target?]\n    # [ways_to_others]     [target_count n-1-ntc ]     [initial_at_others?]\n    \n    def matrix_mul(A, B):\n        return [\n            [(A[0][0] * B[0][0] + A[0][1] * B[1][0]) % MOD,\n             (A[0][0] * B[0][1] + A[0][1] * B[1][1]) % MOD],\n            [(A[1][0] * B[0][0] + A[1][1] * B[1][0]) % MOD,\n             (A[1][0] * B[0][1] + A[1][1] * B[1][1]) % MOD]\n        ]\n    \n    def matrix_pow(matrix, power):\n        if power == 1:\n            return matrix\n        \n        result = [[1, 0], [0, 1]]  # Identity matrix\n        base = matrix\n        \n        while power > 0:\n            if power % 2 == 1:\n                result = matrix_mul(result, base)\n            base = matrix_mul(base, base)\n            power //= 2\n        \n        return result\n    \n    # Create transition matrix\n    # State: [target, non_target]\n    # From target: can go to any of (n-1) non-target positions\n    # From non-target: can go to any of target_count target positions, and (n-1-target_count) non-target positions\n    transition = [\n        [0, target_count],\n        [n - 1, n - 1 - target_count]\n    ]\n    \n    if k == 1:\n        if s == t:\n            return (n - 1) % MOD if 0 in valid_positions else 0\n        else:\n            return target_count % MOD\n    \n    # Compute transition^k\n    final_matrix = matrix_pow(transition, k)\n    \n    # Apply to initial state\n    if s == t:\n        result = (final_matrix[0][0] * 1 + final_matrix[0][1] * 0) % MOD\n    else:\n        result = (final_matrix[0][0] * 0 + final_matrix[0][1] * 1) % MOD\n    \n    return result\n```",
