      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    MOD = 998244353\n    S = input().strip()\n    n = len(S)\n    \n    # dp[i][j] = number of ways to process first i characters with balance j\n    # balance = number of open - number of close\n    dp = [{} for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        for balance, count in dp[i].items():\n            if count == 0:\n                continue\n                \n            char = S[i]\n            if char == '(':\n                new_balance = balance + 1\n                dp[i + 1][new_balance] = (dp[i + 1].get(new_balance, 0) + count) % MOD\n            elif char == ')':\n                if balance > 0:  # Can only place ')' if we have matching '('\n                    new_balance = balance - 1\n                    dp[i + 1][new_balance] = (dp[i + 1].get(new_balance, 0) + count) % MOD\n            else:  # char == '?'\n                # Option 1: treat as '('\n                new_balance = balance + 1\n                dp[i + 1][new_balance] = (dp[i + 1].get(new_balance, 0) + count) % MOD\n                \n                # Option 2: treat as ')' \n                if balance > 0:\n                    new_balance = balance - 1\n                    dp[i + 1][new_balance] = (dp[i + 1].get(new_balance, 0) + count) % MOD\n    \n    # Answer is number of ways to have processed all characters with balance 0\n    print(dp[n].get(0, 0))\n\nsolve()\n```",
