      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the longest subarray where each element appears at most k times. This is a sliding window problem where I'll maintain a window that satisfies the \"good\" condition.\n\nThe approach:\n1. Use two pointers (left and right) to maintain a sliding window\n2. Expand the right pointer and add elements to a frequency map\n3. When any element's frequency exceeds k, shrink the window from the left until the condition is satisfied\n4. Keep track of the maximum window size\n\n```python\ndef maxSubarrayLength(nums, k):\n    left = 0\n    freq_map = {}\n    max_length = 0\n    \n    for right in range(len(nums)):\n        # Add current element to the frequency map\n        freq_map[nums[right]] = freq_map.get(nums[right], 0) + 1\n        \n        # Shrink window while any element's frequency exceeds k\n        while freq_map[nums[right]] > k:\n            freq_map[nums[left]] -= 1\n            if freq_map[nums[left]] == 0:\n                del freq_map[nums[left]]\n            left += 1\n        \n        # Update maximum length\n        max_length = max(max_length, right - left + 1)\n    \n    return max_length\n```",
