      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    n = int(input().strip())\n    s = input().strip()\n    \n    # Set to store unique substrings that are repetitions of one character\n    unique_repetitions = set()\n    \n    i = 0\n    while i < n:\n        # Current character\n        char = s[i]\n        # Count consecutive occurrences of this character\n        count = 0\n        j = i\n        while j < n and s[j] == char:\n            count += 1\n            j += 1\n        \n        # Add all possible repetitions of this character from length 1 to count\n        for length in range(1, count + 1):\n            unique_repetitions.add(char * length)\n        \n        # Move i to the next different character\n        i = j\n    \n    print(len(unique_repetitions))\n\nsolve()\n```",
