    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_314",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nYou are given an integer N and strings R and C of length N consisting of A, B, and C. Solve the following problem.\nThere is a N \\times N grid. All cells are initially empty.\r\nYou can write at most one character from A, B, and C in each cell. (You can also leave the cell empty.)\nDetermine if it is possible to satisfy all of the following conditions, and if it is possible, print one way to do so.\n\n- Each row and each column contain exactly one A, one B, and one C.\n- The leftmost character written in the i-th row matches the i-th character of R.\n- The topmost character written in the i-th column matches the i-th character of C.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\r\nR\r\nC\n\nOutput\n\nIf there is no way to fill the grid to satisfy the conditions in the problem statement, print No in one line.\r\nOtherwise, print one such way to fill the grid in the following format:\nYes\r\nA_1\r\nA_2\r\n\\vdots\r\nA_N\r\n\nThe first line should contain Yes.\r\nThe i-th of the subsequent N lines should contain a string A_i of length N.\n\n- If the j-th character of A_i is ., it indicates that the cell in the i-th row from the top and the j-th column from the left is empty.\n- If the j-th character of A_i is A, it indicates that A is written in the cell in the i-th row from the top and the j-th column from the left.\n- If the j-th character of A_i is B, it indicates that B is written in the cell in the i-th row from the top and the j-th column from the left.\n- If the j-th character of A_i is C, it indicates that C is written in the cell in the i-th row from the top and the j-th column from the left.\n\nIf there are multiple correct ways to fill the grid, you may print any of them.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- N is an integer between 3 and 5, inclusive.\n- R and C are strings of length N consisting of A, B, and C.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n5\r\nABCBC\r\nACAAB\n\nSample Output 1\n\nYes\r\nAC..B\r\n.BA.C\r\nC.BA.\r\nBA.C.\r\n..CBA\r\n\nThe grid in the output example satisfies all the following conditions, so it will be treated as correct.\n\n- Each row contains exactly one A, one B, and one C.\n- Each column contains exactly one A, one B, and one C.\n- The leftmost characters written in the rows are A, B, C, B, C from top to bottom.\n- The topmost characters written in the columns are A, C, A, A, B from left to right.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n3\r\nAAA\r\nBBB\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\r\n\nFor this input, there is no way to fill the grid to satisfy the conditions.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().splitlines()\n    \n    N = int(data[0])\n    R = data[1].strip()\n    C = data[2].strip()\n    \n    # Since N is small (3 to 5), we can use backtracking\n    grid = [['.' for _ in range(N)] for _ in range(N)]\n    \n    # Track counts of A, B, C in each row and column\n    row_count = [{'A': 0, 'B': 0, 'C': 0} for _ in range(N)]\n    col_count = [{'A': 0, 'B': 0, 'C': 0} for _ in range(N)]\n    \n    # Track leftmost and topmost characters\n    row_leftmost = [None] * N\n    col_topmost = [None] * N\n    \n    def is_valid(row, col, char):\n        # Check if placing char at (row, col) violates any constraints\n        if row_count[row][char] >= 1:\n            return False\n        if col_count[col][char] >= 1:\n            return False\n        \n        # Check if this placement would violate leftmost constraint for this row\n        if row_leftmost[row] is None or col < row_leftmost[row][1]:\n            if char != R[row]:\n                return False\n        \n        # Check if this placement would violate topmost constraint for this column\n        if col_topmost[col] is None or row < col_topmost[col][0]:\n            if char != C[col]:\n                return False\n        \n        return True\n    \n    def place(row, col, char):\n        grid[row][col] = char\n        row_count[row][char] += 1\n        col_count[col][char] += 1\n        \n        # Update leftmost for row\n        if row_leftmost[row] is None or col < row_leftmost[row][1]:\n            row_leftmost[row] = (char, col)\n        \n        # Update topmost for column\n        if col_topmost[col] is None or row < col_topmost[col][0]:\n            col_topmost[col] = (char, row)\n    \n    def unplace(row, col, char):\n        grid[row][col] = '.'\n        row_count[row][char] -= 1\n        col_count[col][char] -= 1\n        \n        # Restore leftmost for row\n        if row_leftmost[row] == (char, col):\n            # Recompute leftmost\n            row_leftmost[row] = None\n            for j in range(N):\n                if grid[row][j] != '.':\n                    if row_leftmost[row] is None or j < row_leftmost[row][1]:\n                        row_leftmost[row] = (grid[row][j], j)\n        \n        # Restore topmost for column\n        if col_topmost[col] == (char, row):\n            # Recompute topmost\n            col_topmost[col] = None\n            for i in range(N):\n                if grid[i][col] != '.':\n                    if col_topmost[col] is None or i < col_topmost[col][0]:\n                        col_topmost[col] = (grid[i][col], i)\n    \n    def get_next_cell(row, col):\n        if col == N - 1:\n            return (row + 1, 0)\n        else:\n            return (row, col + 1)\n    \n    def backtrack(row, col):\n        if row == N:\n            # Check if all rows and columns have exactly one A, B, C\n            for i in range(N):\n                if row_count[i]['A'] != 1 or row_count[i]['B'] != 1 or row_count[i]['C'] != 1:\n                    return False\n                if col_count[i]['A'] != 1 or col_count[i]['B'] != 1 or col_count[i]['C'] != 1:\n                    return False\n            return True\n        \n        next_row, next_col = get_next_cell(row, col)\n        \n        # Try leaving the cell empty\n        if backtrack(next_row, next_col):\n            return True\n        \n        # Try placing A, B, C\n        for char in 'ABC':\n            if is_valid(row, col, char):\n                place(row, col, char)\n                if backtrack(next_row, next_col):\n                    return True\n                unplace(row, col, char)\n        \n        return False\n    \n    # First, check immediate contradictions\n    # If any row i must have leftmost character R[i], but C[i] requires a different character at top of column i\n    # We can't put R[i] at (i,0) if some other row j < i needs C[j] to be at (j,i) and it conflicts\n    \n    # Instead of complex upfront checks, use backtracking with the constraints\n    \n    # We need to ensure the leftmost and topmost constraints are respected\n    # Start backtracking from (0,0)\n    if backtrack(0, 0):\n        print(\"Yes\")\n        for i in range(N):\n            print(''.join(grid[i]))\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
