      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minCost(nums, x):\n    n = len(nums)\n    min_costs = nums[:]\n    total_min_cost = sum(nums)\n    \n    for operations in range(1, n):\n        # For each operation, update the minimum cost to collect each chocolate type\n        for i in range(n):\n            # After 'operations' operations, the chocolate originally at position i moves to (i - operations) % n\n            prev_pos = (i - operations) % n\n            # Update minimum cost for chocolate type i\n            min_costs[i] = min(min_costs[i], nums[prevlev_pos])\n        \n        # Calculate total cost for this number of operations\n        total_cost = sum(min_costs) + operations * x\n        total_min_cost = min(total_min_cost, total_cost)\n    \n    return total_min_cost\n```",
