      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nimport heapq\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    N, M = map(int, input().split())\n    items = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        t, x = map(int, input().split())\n        items.append((t, x))\n    \n    # Separate items by type\n    pull_tabs = []  # T=0: directly give happiness\n    regular_cans = []  # T=1: need opener to get happiness\n    openers = []  # T=2: can open up to x cans\n    \n    for t, x in items:\n        if t == 0:\n            pull_tabs.append(x)\n        elif t == 1:\n            regular_cans.append(x)\n        else:  # t == 2\n            openers.append(x)\n    \n    # Sort in descending order for greedy selection\n    pull_tabs.sort(reverse=True)\n    regular_cans.sort(reverse=True)\n    openers.sort(reverse=True)\n    \n    max_happiness = 0\n    \n    # Try different numbers of openers to use (0 to min(M, len(openers)))\n    max_openers = min(M, len(openers))\n    \n    for num_openers in range(max_openers + 1):\n        remaining_slots = M - num_openers\n        if remaining_slots < 0:\n            continue\n            \n        # Calculate happiness with this number of openers\n        happiness = 0\n        \n        # Add happiness from selected openers\n        for i in range(num_openers):\n            happiness += 0  # openers themselves don't give happiness\n        \n        # Calculate how many regular cans we can open\n        total_opens = sum(openers[:num_openers])\n        openable_regular_cans = min(total_opens, remaining_slots, len(regular_cans))\n        \n        # Add happiness from opened regular cans (take the best ones)\n        for i in range(openable_regular_cans):\n            happiness += regular_cans[i]\n        \n        # Remaining slots after using some for regular cans\n        remaining_after_regular = remaining_slots - openable_regular_cans\n        \n        # For pull-tabs and unopened regular cans, we take the best ones for remaining slots\n        candidates = pull_tabs[:]  # pull-tabs always give happiness directly\n        \n        # Add unopened regular cans (they give 0 happiness if not opened)\n        # But we don't add them since they'd give 0\n        \n        # Take best remaining items for remaining slots\n        candidates.sort(reverse=True)\n        for i in range(min(remaining_after_regular, len(candidates))):\n            happiness += candidates[i]\n        \n        max_happiness = max(max_happiness, happiness)\n    \n    # Also consider not using any openers at all\n    # In this case, we can only get happiness from pull-tabs and regular_cans we don't open\n    # Since unopened regular cans give 0 happiness, we only take pull-tabs\n    direct_happiness = 0\n    candidates = pull_tabs[:]\n    candidates.sort(reverse=True)\n    for i in range(min(M, len(candidates))):\n        direct_happiness += candidates[i]\n    \n    max_happiness = max(max_happiness, direct_happiness)\n    \n    # One more approach: try different combinations more systematically\n    max_happiness = 0\n    \n    # For each possible number of openers to pick\n    for num_openers in range(min(M, len(openers)) + 1):\n        if num_openers > M:\n            continue\n            \n        # Calculate maximum openings available\n        total_opens = sum(openers[:num_openers])\n        \n        # We have M - num_openers slots left for pull-tabs and opened regular cans\n        remaining_slots = M - num_openers\n        \n        # We can open at most min(total_opens, remaining_slots, len(regular_cans)) regular cans\n        usable_regular_cans = min(total_opens, remaining_slots, len(regular_cans))\n        \n        # The remaining slots after opening regular cans will be filled with pull-tabs\n        remaining_for_pulltabs = remaining_slots - usable_regular_cans\n        \n        # Calculate happiness\n        happiness = 0\n        \n        # Add happiness from opened regular cans (best ones first)\n        for i in range(usable_regular_cans):\n            happiness += regular_cans[i]\n        \n        # Add happiness from pull-tabs (best ones first)\n        for i in range(min(remaining_for_pulltabs, len(pull_tabs))):\n            happiness += pull_tabs[i]\n        \n        max_happiness = max(max_happiness, happiness)\n    \n    print(max_happiness)\n\nsolve()\n```",
