      "generated_answer": "We use the put-call symmetry relationship for foreign exchange options: the price of a yen-denominated put on dollars can be derived from the dollar-denominated put on yen via a change of numeraire. Using the formula:  \n$ P_y = x^2 e^{-r_y T} \\cdot P_d(x) $ where $ x $ is the exchange rate in $/¥, $ r_y $ is the yen risk-free rate, $ T = 4 $, and adjusting strike and option price accordingly, we compute the price to be approximately 42.77325.  \n\n\\boxed{E}",
