    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We need sequences of consecutive odd integers summing to 240. Let the sequence have \\(n\\) terms, first term \\(a\\) (odd), so sum is \\(\\frac{n}{2}(2a + 2(n-1)) = n(a + n - 1) = 240\\). Therefore \\(n\\) must be a divisor of 240 with \\(n\\) and \\(a = 240/n - n + 1\\) both odd positive integers. Checking divisors of 240 leads to \\(n = 1, 3, 5, 8, 15, 24, 40, 48, 80, 120, 240\\), but only those with \\(a\\) odd and positive give valid sequences, counting yields 8 such sequences.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
