      "generated_answer": "The walking speed is estimated by modeling the leg as a physical pendulum (uniform rod) with period \\(T = 2\\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{2L}{3g}}\\). Substituting \\(L = 3.1\\,\\text{m}\\) and \\(g = 9.8\\,\\text{m/s}^2\\) gives \\(T \\approx 2.886\\,\\text{s}\\). The stride length \\(S = 4.0\\,\\text{m}\\) and speed \\(v = S/T \\approx 1.386\\,\\text{m/s}\\), which rounds to \\(1.4\\,\\text{m/s}\\), corresponding to option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
