      "generated_answer": "The probability that both balls are the same color is calculated as the sum of the probabilities of drawing two green balls or two white balls. There are 7 green and 8 white balls, totaling 15 balls. The number of ways to draw two balls is \\(\\binom{15}{2} = 105\\), the number of ways to draw two green is \\(\\binom{7}{2} = 21\\), and the number of ways to draw two white is \\(\\binom{8}{2} = 28\\). The favorable outcomes are \\(21 + 28 = 49\\), so the probability is \\(\\frac{49}{105} = \\frac{7}{15}\\).\n\n\\boxed{A}",
