      "generated_answer": "The channel matrix is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n0.5 & 0.3 & 0.2 \\\\\n0.2 & 0.3 & 0.5 \\\\\n0.3 & 0.3 & 0.4 \\\\\n\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nEach row corresponds to the output probabilities for a given input symbol. Since inputs are equally probable (each with probability $1/3$), and maximum-likelihood (ML) decoding is used, for each output, we choose the input that maximizes the transition probability to that output. Then, the error probability is the average over all inputs of the probability of not correctly decoding.\n\nCompute the decoding rule per output:\n- Output 1: max at input 1 (0.5), so decode as 1\n- Output 2: all inputs give 0.3, so pick any (assume first, no effect since equal)\n- Output 3: max at input 3 (0.5), so decode as 3\n\nNow compute error probability:\n\nFor input 1: outputs 1:0.5 (correct), 2:0.3 (wrong), 3:0.2 (wrong) → error = 0.3 + 0.2 = 0.5  \nFor input 2: outputs 1:0.2 (wrong), 2:0.3 (tie → assume wrong with prob ≥ 0.3), 3:0.5 (correct). Since output 2 is ambiguous, but ML picks one (say input 1 or 3), so input 2 will be misdecoded when output is 1 or 2 → error = 0.2 + 0.3 = 0.5  \nFor input 3: outputs 1:0.3 (wrong), 2:0.3 (wrong), 3:0.4 (correct) → error = 0.3 + 0.3 = 0.6\n\nAverage error: $ \\frac{1}{3}(0.5 + 0.5 + 0.6) = \\frac{1.6}{3} = \\frac{16}{30} $\n\nThus, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{I}",
