    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the theoretical variance of the random variable with the following probability distribution. x Pr(X = x) 0 (1/4) 1 (1/2) 2 (1/8) 3 (1/8)\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.625\nB. 0.683\nC. 0.350\nD. 1.125\nE. 1.000\nF. 0.500\nG. 0.764\nH. 0.942\nI. 0.859\nJ. 0.725\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, find the mean:  \n\\( \\mu = 0 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} + 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} + 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} = 0 + 0.5 + 0.25 + 0.375 = 1.125 \\).  \n\nThen, variance:  \n\\( \\sigma^2 = (0-1.125)^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} + (1-1.125)^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + (2-1.125)^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} + (3-1.125)^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\)  \n\\( = 1.265625 \\cdot 0.25 + 0.015625 \\cdot 0.5 + 0.765625 \\cdot 0.125 + 3.515625 \\cdot 0.125 \\)  \n\\( = 0.31640625 + 0.0078125 + 0.095703125 + 0.439453125 = 0.859375 \\).  \n\nThus, the variance is approximately 0.859.  \n\n\\boxed{I}",
